### Bookshelf API — click "Send Request" above each block (VS Code REST Client)
@base = http://127.0.0.1:8000/api
@auth = Basic admin:admin12345

### 1. API root
GET {{base}}/

### 2. List books (page 1 of 2)
GET {{base}}/books/

### 3. One book
GET {{base}}/books/3/

### 4. Create without logging in -> 403
POST {{base}}/books/
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Botchan", "author": 2, "published_year": 1906}

### 5. Create with Basic auth -> 201
POST {{base}}/books/
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Botchan", "author": 2, "published_year": 1906}

### 6. Partial update -> 200
PATCH {{base}}/books/6/
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"in_stock": false}

### 7. Validation error -> 400
POST {{base}}/books/
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Future Book", "author": 2, "published_year": 2099, "isbn": "12AB"}

### 8. Delete -> 204
DELETE {{base}}/books/6/
Authorization: {{auth}}

### 9. Search, filter, order
GET {{base}}/books/?search=murakami
###
GET {{base}}/books/?in_stock=false
###
GET {{base}}/books/?published_year__gte=1900&ordering=title
###
GET {{base}}/authors/?country=Japan

### 10. Reviews + average rating
POST {{base}}/reviews/
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"book": 3, "reviewer_name": "Aiko", "rating": 5, "comment": "A classic."}
###
GET {{base}}/books/?ordering=-avg_rating
